<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for May 1.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for May 1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Wednesday announced the following forecasts and data for the period April 29 to May 1.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 29 (actual) 205 mcm, 48 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 30 (forecast) 183 mcm, 43 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>May 1 (forecast) 171 mcm, 40 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 29 (actual) 11.2 Celsius, SNT 11.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 30 (forecast) 13.1 Celsius, SNT 11.2 Celsius</p>
<p>May 1 (forecast) 14.8 Celsius, SNT 11.3 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Wednesday, with none expected on Thursday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
